it's going to say,
instead of just one

00:24:16.310 --> 00:24:20.480
pod for this deployment, I want
five pods for this deployment.

00:24:20.480 --> 00:24:24.660
And then it's going to
spin up all those pods.

00:24:24.660 --> 00:24:27.930
We'll likely catch it here
when it's starting up.

00:24:27.930 --> 00:24:30.680
So you can see, we wanted
five and it started

00:24:30.680 --> 00:24:31.680
creating the other ones.

00:24:31.680 --> 00:24:32.535
Let's hit refresh.

00:24:35.500 --> 00:24:38.440
All right, so now
we've got five replicas

00:24:38.440 --> 00:24:40.540
running of Hello World.

00:24:40.540 --> 00:24:43.270
And we can see that all the
pods associated with this

00:24:43.270 --> 00:24:43.960
are running.

00:24:43.960 --> 00:24:44.830
Now this is great.

00:24:44.830 --> 00:24:48.910
Via the UI, a few clicks, we
just scaled up our application.

00:24:48.910 --> 00:24:50.620
But you know how it is.

00:24:50.620 --> 00:24:53.980
As soon as you think you're
all set, there's a problem

00:24:53.980 --> 00:24:56.050
or there's some new feature
you want to roll out.

00:24:56.050 --> 00:24:57.130
So what we're
going to do next is

00:24:57.130 --> 00:24:58.990
we're actually going
to roll out an update

00:24:58.990 --> 00:25:02.031
to this particular deployment.

00:25:05.250 --> 00:25:07.470
I'm just going to
leave three seconds

00:25:07.470 --> 00:25:11.670
in between as the
different pods spin up.

00:25:11.670 --> 00:25:14.700
And we're going to move
it from 1.0 to 2.0.

00:25:14.700 --> 00:25:17.580
And what should happen
here is at no time

00:25:17.580 --> 00:25:19.692
should we have less
than five pods running.

00:25:19.692 --> 00:25:21.150
And actually, what
it's going to do

00:25:21.150 --> 00:25:23.310
is it's going to
roll the updates.

00:25:23.310 --> 00:25:27.300
So it'll spin up a 2.0 pod
and shut down a 1.0 pod.

00:25:27.300 --> 00:25:30.120
And then spin up another
2.0, and shut down a 1.0,

00:25:30.120 --> 00:25:32.460
so that we always have at
least five replicas running

00:25:32.460 --> 00:25:33.630
at any one point of time.

00:25:36.790 --> 00:25:39.490
We're rolling out the updates,
and you see that-- actually, we

00:25:39.490 --> 00:25:40.575
had those five running.

00:25:40.575 --> 00:25:42.200
And we start getting
some more running,

00:25:42.200 --> 00:25:46.390
because we're seeing this
rolling state as some spin up

00:25:46.390 --> 00:25:50.140
and some shut down from
the old version, 1.0,

00:25:50.140 --> 00:25:51.060
to the new version.

00:25:54.180 --> 00:25:58.230
You can see the deployment
is gone, but some of the pods

00:25:58.230 --> 00:25:58.980
are still running.

00:26:04.010 --> 00:26:05.630
It's going to take
another few more

00:26:05.630 --> 00:26:08.770
seconds before the old
pods get shut down.

00:26:11.560 --> 00:26:13.660
Some of them are starting
to shut down there.

00:26:25.670 --> 00:26:29.960
All right, so now
we've done the update.

00:26:29.960 --> 00:26:33.440
This particular deployment has
five of the new pods running.

00:26:33.440 --> 00:26:38.510
And we've updated
the application.

00:26:38.510 --> 00:26:40.190
So that's the second demo.

00:26:40.190 --> 00:26:42.470
And now we're going to
switch back to the slides.

00:26:48.422 --> 00:26:50.350
Can you switch us back
to the slides, please?

00:26:53.110 --> 00:26:54.430
Thank you.

00:26:54.430 --> 00:26:58.900
All right, so Matt talked
a bit about the velocity,

00:26:58.900 --> 00:27:02.050
as well as where people
have their infrastructure

00:27:02.050 --> 00:27:03.100
and need to be running.

00:27:03.100 --> 00:27:08.140
And then Amr dug into Anthos
and really an overview of many

00:27:08.140 --> 00:27:09.422
of the different components.

00:27:09.422 --> 00:27:11.380
And then I went through
and actually showed you

00:27:11.380 --> 00:27:14.290
a demo about connecting
your clusters to Google,

00:27:14.290 --> 00:27:15.940
as well as
interacting with them.

00:27:19.353 --> 00:27:20.770
That's really the
end of the talk.

00:27:20.770 --> 00:27:23.290
And we want to open it
up now for questions,

00:27:23.290 --> 00:27:25.780
as well as invite
you to come talk

00:27:25.780 --> 00:27:29.290
to us either after this talk,
as well as at the reception

00:27:29.290 --> 00:27:30.640
this evening.

00:27:30.640 --> 00:27:33.190
We do have people
here all week as well

00:27:33.190 --> 00:27:35.890
at KubeCon, in the
Community Lounge,

00:27:35.890 --> 00:27:38.940
as well as in the booth.

00:27:38.940 --> 00:27:40.530
Thank you, everyone.

